WHAT IT IS. Not a Slovak structure: it is the EU OSS VAT return,
targetNamespace urn:ec.europa.eu:taxud:frsr:vatunion:v1.0, root
OSSVATReturnMSCON, version="1.0" on xsd:schema. That stamp is the EU
structure's version, not a revision of this file, and nothing validates it —
the digest above is what detects a silent revision.

THE PREFIX MATTERS. The eForm's XML loader (Scripts/form.555.xmlfdf.js,
function loadxmlfinal) finds elements by qualified name
('vun:OSSVATReturnMSCON', 'vun:TraderID', ...). A document in a default
namespace validates against this schema and loads into the portal form as
an empty return. The template emits the `vun:` prefix for that reason.

OTHER SCHEMES. Probed 2026-09-28: dposs_ioss01.xsd and dposs_neu01.xsd are
404 (with the ~1 245-byte HTML error page — test by status code, never by
size). The import and non-Union returns are not built here.

REFRESH PROCEDURE
  1. Fetch the ekr URL above and compare the md5 with the first line.
  2. Check the status code, not the size.
  3. Open the eForm page and check which XSD it references (grep '.xsd'); a
     new vzor would appear as a new DPOSS_EUvNN form with a new schema name.
  4. If the digest moved: replace data/dposs_eu01.xsd, update this file, and
     re-read form.555.xmlfdf.js (createxmlfinal) for changes to element
     order or to what the portal leaves out — the template mirrors it.
